rt protocol is strong: it records a healthy baseline, acknowledgement, observed disconnect, changed boot identity, recovered account/home/login behavior, and matches the fixed lifecycle boot observations. Hygiene is slightly reduced by one abandoned temporary restart log.","limitations":["The captured passwd and shadow values are redacted, so exact fields are supported by successful command assertions and displayed derived state rather than visible raw entries.","The generic failed-services lifecycle probe is unsupported on Alpine; recovery is instead supported by command execution, OpenRC's default runlevel, restored SSH/DHCP listeners, and the task-specific post-restart checks."]}
